Add({
	id = "the-deadmines",
	title = "The Deadmines",
	aliases = { "Deadmines" },
	faction = "Alliance",
	continent = "Eastern Kingdoms",
	zone = "The Deadmines",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "zone" },
	},
	regionKind = "dungeon",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Deadmines lie beneath the village of {link:moonbrook}Moonbrook{/link} in {link:westfall}Westfall{/link}. Once they were the richest gold works in the human lands. Now they are the secret heart of the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias Brotherhood{/link}. In their depths, the stonemasons of {link:edwin-vancleef}Edwin VanCleef{/link} and the goblins they have hired are building something that no one in {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} has yet seen: a great warship, hidden in a sea cave at the bottom of the mines.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[For generations the mines beneath {link:moonbrook}Moonbrook{/link} sent gold to the treasury of the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link}. When the {link:horde}Horde{/link} razed {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} in the {link:first-war}First War{/link}, the miners fled and the works fell silent. The tunnels were left to the dark, and folk began to call them the Deadmines. They remained empty through the years of exile and rebuilding. When the betrayed masons came west, they found a fortress already dug for them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The Brotherhood has made the old mine its sanctum. {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias{/link} miners dig in its shafts, and wizards and evokers of the Brotherhood guard its halls. Goblin craftsmen and engineers of the Brotherhood's hire cut timber, smelt metal and assemble machines. An {link:ogres}ogre{/link} keeps the first gate. Far below, where the tunnels open onto the sea, the ship is nearly ready, and its captain and crew wait for their master's command. What {link:edwin-vancleef}VanCleef{/link} means to do with it, only the Brotherhood knows. Many fear that it is meant for {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Within the Mines",
			text = [=[• {b}The Collapsed Wing.{/b} Before the Brotherhood's entrance, a side passage leads to tunnels where a party of dwarven miners and explorers was buried when the roof fell. They do not rest. Their dead still walk the dark with picks and dynamite.
• {b}The Mast Room.{/b} Here the goblins of the lumbermaster {link:sneed}Sneed{/link} cut great timbers for the ship.
• {b}The Foundry.{/b} Here the goblin {link:gilnid}Gilnid{/link} smelts the metal of the mines.
• {b}{link:ironclad-cove}Ironclad Cove{/link}.{/b} At the bottom of the mines lies a cave open to the sea, where the Brotherhood's ship rides at anchor. Its gate is sealed, and only powder and cannon will open it.
• {b}The Hidden Way Out.{/b} From the cove, a passage climbs to the hills behind {link:moonbrook}Moonbrook{/link}, near the sea.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Those Who Dwell Below",
			text = [=[The Brotherhood's servants here are many. The foreman {link:rhahkzor}Rhahk'Zor{/link}, the goblins {link:sneed}Sneed{/link} and {link:gilnid}Gilnid{/link}, and the ship's crew under {link:captain-greenskin}Captain Greenskin{/link} all answer to {link:edwin-vancleef}Edwin VanCleef{/link}. Rarer dangers also lurk in the tunnels, among them a miner of great strength known as Miner Johnson.]=],
		},
	},
})

